Follow the ntfy gateway's contract (ntfy.sliccy.ai, sliccy-ai#42/#47) in the client.

Reason: upstream's client (client/client.go handleSubscribeConnLoop) says
"The retry logic is crude and may lose messages": after a dropped stream it
waits 10 s and reconnects with the original options, so it loses or repeats
messages, and it ignores Retry-After. The gateway drops a subscriber that
falls 1 MiB behind and answers 429 with retry-after: 60. This patch:
- remembers the last message id of each subscription and reconnects with
  since=<last id> (since=<time of the open event> before the first message),
  skipping a repeat of the last message, so a drop loses and repeats nothing;
- waits max(10 s, Retry-After) before reconnecting after a 429;
- ends ntfy sub with a non-zero exit on 401 or 403 (a forged, revoked or
  wrongly scoped token), instead of retrying every 10 s for ever;
- retries a publish after a 429 with Retry-After, waiting that long, at most
  twice, when the body can be re-sent (a message or a --file); otherwise, or
  after more than 5 minutes, it fails and names the wait;
- refuses a message over 1 MiB (arguments, --message or stdin) before any
  request, where upstream silently cut stdin at 1 MiB; --file attachments
  are not capped by the client;
- reads stream lines up to 4 MiB (upstream: bufio.Scanner's 64 KiB) and
  reports a scanner error, so one over-long line cannot loop a since= resume.

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: upstream's subscribe loop resumes with since=, honours
Retry-After and stops on auth errors, and publish refuses oversize messages.

